    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Figured bass (thoroughbass) is Baroque shorthand for harmony above a bass line — foundation of 17th–18th century accompaniment."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "figures",
      "title": "Figures",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Numbers below bass indicate intervals above bass note to play. 5/3 = root position triad. 6 = first inversion. 6/4 = second inversion. 7 = seventh chord. Accidentals alter figures."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "realisation",
      "title": "Realisation",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Keyboardist improvises chord voicings from figures + bass. Harpsichord, organ, or lute with cello/bassoon on bass line."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "modern-relevance",
      "title": "Modern relevance",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Understanding figures clarifies Bach harmonic analysis. Jazz chord symbols are distant descendants. Roman numeral analysis partially replaces figures today."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
